---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BranchRivers from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/BranchRivers.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import lines from "../data/lines.json";

/* 11 October 2026. Asked for by David after seeing Defranceski's «Six families,
   one surname»: did this archive have a picture like that? It had none, and
   Uroda is the surname that needed it — three groups at Karlobag, a dead man of
   Šibenik, and two Dalmatian families of the index all answer to the one name,
   and a reader (or this archive) who met «Dume Uroda» twice would have merged
   them.

   The drawing is the kit's BranchRivers, which three archives had already
   drawn by hand. The unplaced and loose footers are passed empty and listed
   below the figure instead, with a sentence and a link each, which is more than
   the figure can hold and keeps them on the page. WHAT IS THIS ARCHIVE'S ALONE
   is the data, and the rule: a lane is a family the registers show, a dotted
   bridge is a join no document makes, and nothing is merged until one does. */
const set = lines.sets[0];
const snap = (id) => u(`/snapshots/#${id}`);
---
<Base title="The Lines of a Name"
      eyebrow="Uroda — six groups, one surname"
      dek={set.dek}>

  <section class="blk">
    <p class="lede">
      They are not one family, and nothing read so far says they were. The same name turns up at
      Karlobag in three households, in the mouth of a dead man «of Šibenik», and in two Dalmatian
      families of the index. <strong>So each gets a lane of its own.</strong> What is documented
      goes on the lane; a join between lanes is drawn dotted and says what it rests on; nothing is
      merged until a register joins it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <figure class="rivers">
      <BranchRivers rivers={{ ...set, unplaced: [], loose: [] }} caption="" />
      <figcaption>
        Hover or tab any dot and it says what the register behind it says; click again to go there.
        <strong>The top lane is the only one this archive descends from.</strong> The dotted curves
        are candidate joins between lanes, on evidence short of a document: «same name, Šibenik»
        and «the 1742 son» are questions, not findings. A dotted end-point is a hope, not a link.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="note"><strong>One spelling is not a search.</strong> The registers write
    <em>Uroda</em>, <em>urode</em>, <em>vrode</em>, <em>Urodan</em>, <em>Urada</em>; the index
    reads one Karlobag father as <em>Sime</em>, and one Drniš father four ways (<em>Janpao,
    Ganpas, Pompio, Tomaso</em>). At Karlobag in 1734 a priest writes <strong>«Dume urode alliti
    Horaca»</strong> — a by-name — and before the 1730s the book has <em>no</em> Uroda at all, so
    a baptism of the man himself would sit under another surname. See
    <a href={u("/by-names/")}>The Second Name</a>.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="blk" id="lines">
    <div class="lab">What each line stands on</div>
    <h2>The six groups, and the pages behind them</h2>
    {set.lanes.map((l) => (
      <div class="qa" id={l.key} style="margin:1.3rem 0">
        <h3 style={`color:${l.colour}`}>{l.label}</h3>
        <p class="dim mono" style="font-size:.78rem">{l.conf}</p>
        <ol style="margin:.5rem 0 0;padding-left:1.2rem">
          {l.nodes.map(([place, year, why]) => (
            <li style="margin:.35rem 0"><strong>{place}</strong> · <span class="mono">{year}</span> — {why}</li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        {set.sources[l.key]?.length > 0 && (
          <p style="margin-top:.7rem">The pages themselves:
            {set.sources[l.key].map(([label, id], i) => (
              <>{i ? " · " : " "}<a href={snap(id)}>{label}</a></>
            ))}
          </p>
        )}
        {l.ends.map(([e, , why]) => (
          <p class="dim" style="margin:.4rem 0 0">→ <strong>{e}</strong>: {why}</p>
        ))}
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <h2>Real households of the name, not yet on any lane</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left:1.1rem">
      {set.unplaced.map(([name, href, why]) => (
        <li style="margin:.4rem 0"><a href={u(href)}><strong>{name}</strong></a> — {why}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <h2 style="margin-top:1.6rem">Attached to no line here</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left:1.1rem">
      {set.loose.map(([name, href, why]) => (
        <li style="margin:.4rem 0"><a href={u(href)}><strong>{name}</strong></a> — {why}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="blk">
    <div class="note"><strong>What each lane owes.</strong> A lane carries three things: what is
    documented, what is inferred, and <em>what would have to be found to join it to another</em>.
    For Uroda that is: <strong>Dume's baptism</strong> (likely under the by-name, in the 1700s),
    <strong>the marriage of Georgius and Maria</strong> (not in Karlobag's marriage book 1736–1804;
    perhaps Dalmatia), <strong>Maria's maiden name</strong> (the 1764 godparents Barach and
    Margvart are only candidates), and <strong>the Šibenik and Drniš baptisms themselves</strong>.
    The full list is on <a href={u("/worklist/")}>the work list</a>. The Karlobag mother-side
    surnames — Pilipić, Smojver, Gerkacs, Bacchi, Luckinić — will get the same page when each has
    a second family of its name to be told apart from.</div>
  </section>

</Base>
